{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>נקי יהיה לביתו.</b> Rashi explained: 'also for his house' — to include his vineyard. It seems to me this is what we learn in Mishnah Sotah, chapter משוח מלחמה: And these do not move from their place — one who built a house and dedicated it, one who planted a vineyard and redeemed it, and one who marries his betrothed, and one who takes in his yevamah. As it is said: נקי יהיה לביתו — this is his house; 'יהיה' — to include his vineyard; ושמח את אשתו — this is his wife whom he takes, to include his yevamah. And all of these are not supplied with water and food, and the roads are not repaired for them, for they are נקיים from everything."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:19.473627268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}